/*  Install Allure Report 

1. To install the Allure    - npm install -g allure-commandline
2. To Execute superate test - &particularTest& --reporter=line,allure-playwright
3. To Generate the Report   - allure generate ./allure-results --clean -o ./allure-report
3.  To open the allure       - allure open ./allure-report

*/




/*   Jenkins Setups

1. Download the .War file 
2. open the commandline then run the "java -jar jenkins.war"
3. Open the localhost:8080 the port where it is running
4. Go to the New item 
5. Free stype 
 
 If you are running it in the Local file not in Git level then flow this steps for configration
 
 1. Go to configration
 2. Advance 
 3. Custume work space 
 4. paste the "locater of the folder"
 5. Add Build step--> Execute window batch commandline
 6. Execute the Script in package.json "npm run regression"
 7. BUILD NOW

*/


/*   Install Cucumber

1. Run this commandline "npm install @cucumber/cucumber" installed the package
2. Install the plugin like extention "cucumber(Gherkin)"

*/ 


/*parameterization, parllel, html report, rerun faild test
1. Scenario Outline : which means this test gonna execute multiple time
2. npx cucumber-js features/Ecommerce.feature --parallel 2   - execute the feature file parllelly 
3. Examples:
      | userName           | passWord       |
      | rahulshettyacademy | Learning@830$3mK2 |
      | Hello@123          | Test123        | 
      parameterization to execute with multiple set of data alosng with 1st point
4. HTML Report - --format html:cucumber r-report.html  
5. Return Test case - --retry 1 (npx cucumber-js --tags "@regression" --ertry 1 )
6. Tags - "@regression"
*/




